# `Math.max(1, value)`: the call is made in line behind conversions of its operands. A conversion throws for a symbol and runs the program's valueOf for an object:
# it names the built-in in whose place it stands, so that a stack lists `max`; written in tail position it bears the mark of the tail call, so that the function that left is not listed.
